        <article>
          <h1>Install</h1>
          <p>Baudelaire is a single binary with no runtime dependencies. The Typst compiler is built in, so there is nothing else to install.</p>
          <h3>With cargo</h3>
          <pre><code data-lang="sh"><span style="color: #e5d006">cargo</span> install baudelaire</code></pre>
          <p>This builds from source and drops the <code>baudelaire</code> binary in <code>~/.cargo/bin</code>. Confirm it works:</p>
          <pre><code data-lang="sh"><span style="color: #e5d006">baudelaire</span><span style="color: #e5d008"> --</span><span style="color: #e5d006">version</span></code></pre>
          <div class="callout callout-note">
            <p class="callout-label">NOTE</p>
            Fonts come from your system. On a slim server or CI image, install a font package such as <code>fonts-dejavu</code> so Typst has something to render with.
          </div>
          <h3>From a release</h3>
          <p>Prebuilt binaries for Linux, macOS, and Windows are attached to every <a href="https://github.com/cestef/baudelaire/releases">GitHub release</a>. Download the archive for your platform, extract it, and put the binary on your <code>PATH</code>.</p>
          <p>Next: <a href="/guide/quickstart/">the quickstart</a>.</p>
